# CG

Display name is **CG** (broadcast Character Generator). Keep it. Do **not** rename to Overlay, Graphics, GFX, Live, Board, or Item.

This is the locked vocabulary for code, UI copy, DB, routes, and the subdomain. If a new Element needs a payload key, add it under `payload` jsonb — do not invent a parallel table or a second token scheme.

| Surface | Locked name |
|---|---|
| Launcher / `tyapp_app_feature.name` | `CG` |
| Route | `/cg` (`/cg/list`, `/cg/new`, `/cg/edit/:id`, `/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId`) |
| Overlay path | `/o/:token` on the CG host; fallback `/cg-live/:token` on Jaxfr |
| Subdomain | `cg` → `https://cg.tszyin.com` / `http://cg.localhost:4200` |
| Code | `features/cg/`, `apps/cg/` (overlay), `core/domains/cg/` |
| Panel files | `cg-package-edit.*` (skeleton is `*-edit`; the page is still Panel) |
| Layer desk | `cg-layer-edit.*` nested on the Panel at `/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId` (same right column as tiles — not a second page) |

## UI words

| Word | Means | Example |
|---|---|---|
| **Package** | One look to use together | CH36, News SNG |
| **Element** | Kind in the catalog (code registry `CG_ELEMENT_CATALOG`) | Logo, Clock, Ticker |
| **Layer** | One instance inside a Package | CH36's Logo |
| **Panel** | This Package's operator page | Left Package (main), right Layers |
| **Output** | OBS URL (full-frame transparent Stage) | Package Output (default), Layer Output |
| **Stage** | 16:9 canvas | Tile thumbs, On air / Pending, overlay |
| **On air** | Last Save (plus live cue) | Small monitor of what OBS has |
| **Pending** | Unsaved draft mix | Save promotes it to On air |

**Channel / Source** stay on the Package as `role`. Clock is not Timer. Overlay is the public page implementation, not a product noun. Welcome → CG and every CG subpage (list / Panel) skip the Jaxfr page crossfade — instant swap, no 200ms fade. Other Jaxfr features keep the Aero transition.

**Panel layout:** one page, two columns. Left is the **Package** (main): column title, then Pending | On air, then Package controls. Right is **Layers** (inside that Package): column title + catalog, tiles, and the selected Layer desk (`/cg/edit/:id/layer/:layerId` is that selection, not a separate layout). Click the selected tile again to close the desk. Package title is heavier than Layers — Stage / Appear / Look stay as inner kickers, not column labels.

**Always desktop:** list + Panel lock the viewport to `width=1280` and `min-width: 1280px`. Phone and tablet keep the same 3-pane (pinch-zoom / horizontal pan) — do not add a stacked `@media` reflow. Overlay `/o` and `/cg-live` stay `width=device-width`. Unlock the viewport when leaving CG admin.

**No fixed palette — CG follows the operator's own Aero/Material + light/dark choice:** an earlier pass gave CG admin a fixed "broadcast console" identity (`_cg-theme.scss`); that was reverted (2026-09-24) after live review — the user wants the traditional skeuomorphic 3D "Windows 7 Aero / iOS 6" button look for themselves, but their partner prefers flat Material, and the app's existing per-user `visual_theme`/`color_mode` toggle (`UserPreferenceService`/`ThemeService`) already resolves that tension app-wide. CG does not need — and must not reintroduce — a third, fixed identity. `_cg-theme.scss` and its `console-light`/`console-dark` mixins are deleted; do not recreate them.

**Buttons are real Angular Material components, not hand-rolled `<button class="cg-btn">`:** every action/toggle button in CG (`cg-package-list`, `cg-package-edit`, `cg-layer-edit`) uses `mat-stroked-button` / `mat-flat-button` / `mat-icon-button` with a shared compact `.cg-seg-btn` (28-32px tall) sizing class, plus `.cg-seg-btn.selected` for the active option in a toggle group (Alpha/Studio, Channel/Source, Fade/Cut, Color/B&W, Inherit/Color/B&W, News/Show, Cue Fade/Cut). This gets the Windows-Aero glossy 3D gradient (or flat Material pill, in Material mode) for free from `src/app/styles/_aero-controls.scss`, since CG's routes are nested inside `<app-layout>`. Do not hand-roll a new button look for CG — mirror this pattern for any new button. **Exception:** a file-picker trigger must be a real `<button mat-stroked-button>` whose `(click)` calls `.click()` on a visually-hidden sibling `<input type="file">` via a template ref (e.g. `#logoFileInput`) — Angular Material's button directives do not attach to `<label>`, so `<label mat-stroked-button>` silently renders as unstyled plain text (see `cg-layer-edit.html`'s "Choose local image" / "Load .txt / .srt" for the working pattern). The on/off Layer switch (`.cg-switch`) stays hand-rolled on purpose: `--mdc-switch-*` CSS custom properties don't shrink `mat-slide-toggle`'s footprint, and it has a different (checkmark-in-thumb) visual language than this app's pill toggle.

**No global toolbar, still:** the global `<app-toolbar>` is hidden entirely for `/cg` and `/cg/*` routes (`isCgAdminPath()` in `core/domains/cg/cg.util.ts`, wired into `Layout.shouldShowToolbar()` next to Daily Log's exclusion) — this part of the original decision stands, independent of the palette reversal above. Back / Save-or-Create / Delete / sync-status live inline in the left Package column's header (`.cg-col-head`) instead; list page gets its own inline Home / Refresh / New package row.

## Tables and columns (final)

`tyapp_cg_package` PK `tb_tyapp_cgpk_id` (seq `tb_tyapp_cgpk_seq_no`):

`name`, `role` (`channel` \| `source`), `public_token`, `duration_ms` (`0` = cut, default `400` = fade), `look` (`color` \| `mono`), `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`

`tyapp_cg_layer` PK `tb_tyapp_cgly_id` (seq `tb_tyapp_cgly_seq_no`):

`package_id` → package PK, `element_type`, `public_token`, `layout` jsonb, `payload` jsonb, `visible` (On/Off), `look` (`inherit` \| `color` \| `mono`; default `inherit` = Package Look), `sort_order`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`

Layout jsonb: `x`, `y`, `unit` (`percent` \| `px`), `anchor`, `scale`, `width`, `height`. Logo `scale` is a CSS transform of the box. Subtitle `scale` only multiplies type size (`1` = ffmpeg FontSize 16.1 / PlayRes 288, about 5.6% of frame height); Show preset Scale 1 is about 7.2% of frame height. The caption stays inside `width` and wraps. Overlay uses `vh` so Browser Source gets on-air size even when `cqh` does not. News look is white fill, regular weight, `ScaleY` 1.11, `Spacing` 1.68. Black outline is a **behind** `-webkit-text-stroke` copy (fill sits on top). Do not put stroke and fill on the same span — OBS CEF has no `paint-order`, and 8-way `text-shadow` makes a jagged octagon around CJK. Show is larger, slightly gold, thicker behind-stroke. Latin runs use Segoe UI / Arial; CJK stays 華康中黑體 / JhengHei.

Logo payload jsonb: `imageUrl`, `fileName`

Subtitle payload jsonb: `lines` (string[]), `index` (`number` \| `null` = blank / off air), `cursor` (last clicked row; kept when Blank), `style.preset` (`news` \| `show`; default `news`), `transition.duration_ms` (cue crossfade; `0` = cut, default `400`). This is **not** Package Appear.

Tokens share one `/o/:token` space (unique across both tables in practice). Do not add a token table.

RPCs: `tyapp_cg_package_soft_delete_single_record`, `tyapp_cg_layer_soft_delete_single_record`, `tyapp_cg_get_output_by_token`.

**Save** writes the Package and applies it to Output. Each Layer **fades in or out on its own** using the Package `duration_ms` (`0` = cut). Layers that did not change stay put — turning Weather On does not blink an already-On Logo. Panel tile order is Stage **z-order** (first tile behind, last in front); drag to reorder, Save to apply.

**Host vs inner:** Package / Panel owns mix — which Layers exist, On/Off, z-order, OBS URL, **Appear** (Fade / Cut + `duration_ms` for the whole Layer going on or off), and **Package Look** as a master bus. Package B&W greys **every** Layer. Package Color lets a Layer set Inherit / Color / B&W (B&W = that Layer grey). Layer Color cannot punch out of a B&W Package. Layer desk does **not** have its own Appear. Cue crossfade, News / Show, layout, and later inner animation live on the Layer (`payload.transition.duration_ms` for cue). Package Cut must not force cue to cut.

**On air / Pending:** the Panel shows **two small** 16:9 Stages of the **full mix**, **Pending on the left**, **On air on the right** (top-left pane). **On air** is last Save (OBS). **Pending** is the unsaved draft. Save copies Pending onto On air. New unsaved Package: On air is empty. Live cue (Up / Down / Blank / Paste / Load) **and Cue Fade / Cut** also update On air immediately; unsaved News / Show / layout / Look / On/Off wait for Save. Alpha / Studio is shared by both monitors.

**Save scope is unchanged, still Package-gated:** Package Save applies name, role, Appear (`duration_ms`), Package Look, **and** every Layer's existence / On-Off / z-order / layout / Layer Look / News-Show style — none of that is instant, including toggling a Layer On/Off. This was discussed and deliberately kept (an operator flipping a problem Layer off mid-broadcast still clicks Save to commit it) — do not make Layer On/Off or Package Look instant. The only live exception is the pre-existing subtitle cue behavior described above.

**Layer desk has its own small Pending/On-air pair:** in addition to the Package-level monitors in the left column, the selected Layer's desk (right column) shows a second, smaller Pending/On-air `app-cg-mix-preview` pair scoped to just that one Layer (`[layers]="[layer]"` for Pending, the matching row from `cg.onAirLayers()` for On air — empty until that Layer has been saved once). This has its own local Alpha/Studio toggle; it does not replace or resize the Package-level monitors.

Greyscale is per-layer host filter with Package `duration_ms`; it must not change z-order.

**Subtitle cue is the live exception:** Up / Down / click / Paste / Load .txt or .srt patches only `lines` / `index` / `cursor` immediately (no Package Save). Cue Fade / Cut patches `payload.transition.duration_ms` the same way (`0` = cut, default `400`) — it is **not** Package Appear, and it does **not** wait for Save. Unsaved News/Show must not leak to OBS. Overlay polls every 300ms and shows `lines[index]`. Cue changes **crossfade** with that Layer duration; this is inside the caption, not Layer On/Off opacity. `index = null` is blank air; `cursor` stays on the last clicked row so Down continues from there and Up puts it back. SRT import strips sequence numbers and timestamps; each cue becomes one queue line. Subtitle desk shows Cue Fade/Cut next to Up / Down / Blank, then Scale / Y / Width (bottom-center, `%`), plus News / Show. Logo still has full X/Y/Width/Scale/Anchor/Unit.

**Copy Layer** INSERTs a new row into another Package: new PK, new `public_token` (never share the OBS URL), `index = null`. Additive SQL: `supabase/sql/cg-layer-look.sql`.

Do not revive `tyapp_cg_slot` or `component_type`.
